<details>
<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (3)</summary><blockquote>

<details>
<summary>app/init/resources.php (3)</summary><blockquote>

`603-625`: **Cache key construction duplicates `EventProcessor` logic.**

Lines 614-622 duplicate the cache key format from `EventProcessor.getFunctionsEvents()`. If the key format changes, both locations must be updated, creating a maintenance burden.

Consider extracting a public method in `EventProcessor` to build the cache key, or passing `EventProcessor` to this listener.



<details>
<summary>♻️ Suggested approach</summary>

Add a public method to `EventProcessor`:

```php
// In EventProcessor.php
public function getFunctionEventsCacheKey(Document $project, Database $dbForProject): string
{
    $hostname = $dbForProject->getAdapter()->getHostname();
    return \sprintf(
        '%s-cache-%s:%s:%s:project:%s:functions:events',
        $dbForProject->getCacheName(),
        $hostname ?? '',
        $dbForProject->getNamespace(),
        $dbForProject->getTenant(),
        $project->getId()
    );
}
```

Then inject `EventProcessor` and call the method in the listener.
</details>

---

`568-598`: **Add error handling to prevent listener exceptions from breaking database operations.**

If any of the queue operations (`trigger()`) throw an exception, it will propagate to the database operation and potentially cause a failed transaction or data inconsistency. Wrap the listener body in a try-catch block.


<details>
<summary>🛡️ Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
 $eventDatabaseListener = function (Document $project, Document $document, Response $response, Event $queueForEvents, Func $queueForFunctions, Webhook $queueForWebhooks, Realtime $queueForRealtime) {
+    try {
         // Only trigger events for user creation with the database listener.
         if ($document->getCollection() !== 'users') {
             return;
         }

         $queueForEvents
             ->setEvent('users.[userId].create')
             ->setParam('userId', $document->getId())
             ->setPayload($response->output($document, Response::MODEL_USER));

         // Trigger functions, webhooks, and realtime events
         $queueForFunctions
             ->from($queueForEvents)
             ->trigger();


         /** Trigger webhooks events only if a project has them enabled */
         if (!empty($project->getAttribute('webhooks'))) {
             $queueForWebhooks
                 ->from($queueForEvents)
                 ->trigger();
         }

         /** Trigger realtime events only for non console events */
         if ($queueForEvents->getProject()->getId() !== 'console') {
             $queueForRealtime
                 ->from($queueForEvents)
                 ->trigger();
         }
+    } catch (\Throwable $e) {
+        Console::error('Event database listener error: ' . $e->getMessage());
+    }
 };
```
</details>

---

`627-732`: **Add error handling to `usageDatabaseListener`.**

Similar to `eventDatabaseListener`, this listener lacks try-catch protection. An exception from `queueForStatsUsage` operations could propagate and break the database operation.


<details>
<summary>🛡️ Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
 $usageDatabaseListener = function (string $event, Document $document, StatsUsage $queueForStatsUsage) {
+    try {
         $value = 1;

         switch ($event) {
             // ... existing switch logic ...
         }

         switch (true) {
             // ... existing switch logic ...
         }
+    } catch (\Throwable $e) {
+        Console::error('Usage database listener error: ' . $e->getMessage());
+    }
 };
```
</details>

</blockquote></details>

</blockquote></details>

